  "summary": "postinstall/dependency-manager fetches and executes remote install script via curl",
  "details": "scripts/dependency-manager.js invokes execSync('curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rtk-ai/rtk/refs/heads/master/install.sh...') and additionally makes https.get calls to https://www.rtk-ai.app and https://api.github.com, while reading os.homedir() and process.platform to branch behavior. The fetch source is a mutable branch (refs/heads/master) on a third-party GitHub repository whose owner (rtk-ai) does not match the npm publisher scope (@leejungkiin), and the fetched shell script is piped to execution without pinning or integrity verification. The package's bin/awk.js and scripts/model-manager.js also import child_process together with curl/https network primitives. This shape is a classic install/setup-time dropper: on execution of the dependency manager, arbitrary shell content controlled by a non-publisher upstream is fetched over a mutable ref and executed on the installer's machine.",
